The test vehicle approaches the intersection at target speed V1. The cyclist waiting to cross the pedestrian crossing are positioned on the left/right side of the vertical lane to the right. The distance between the cyclist and the lane centerline is D. The cyclist crosses the pedestrian crossing from the left/right side of the current lane at speed V2. During the test vehicle's right turn through the intersection, the time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the cyclist to reach the collision point.